from az_lib import *
# ---- 1 Microsoft Entra users and groups
C(1,"Security group vs Microsoft 365 group?","**Security group:** grants access to resources (Azure roles, apps, licenses). Members can be users, devices, service principals and other groups. **Microsoft 365 group:** collaboration (shared mailbox, calendar, SharePoint, Teams). Members are users only.")
C(1,"Assigned vs dynamic membership?","**Assigned:** an admin adds and removes members by hand. **Dynamic user / dynamic device:** a rule on attributes (for example `user.department -eq \"Sales\"`) adds and removes members automatically. Dynamic groups need **Microsoft Entra ID P1**, and you **cannot add members by hand**.")
C(1,"How do you create many users at once?","**Bulk create** in the Entra admin center: download the CSV template, fill it, upload it. PowerShell (Microsoft Graph) and the Graph API also work.")
C(1,"What must be set on a user before you assign a license?","The **usage location** (country). Some services are not available in every country, so a license cannot be assigned without it.")
C(1,"Group-based licensing: what is it and what does it need?","Assign a license to a **group** and every member gets it; members who leave lose it. Needs a paid Entra plan such as **P1** (or Microsoft 365 E3/Business Premium). Errors show per user, for example when no licenses are left.")
C(1,"How do external (B2B) users work?","You **invite** them with their own email. They sign in with **their own** identity (work account, Microsoft account, Google, one-time passcode). They appear as **UserType: Guest** and get access you grant, like any other user.")
C(1,"SSPR: what license does password reset need, and who can configure it?","Self-service password **reset** needs **Microsoft Entra ID P1** (password *change* is free for cloud users). Writeback to on-premises needs P1/P2. Configure it as an **Authentication Policy Administrator**, scoped to **None, Selected (one group), or All**.")
C(1,"SSPR for administrators?","Admin accounts are **always enabled** for SSPR and **always need two methods** (a two-gate policy). You cannot turn that off for admins with the SSPR scope setting.")
C(1,"What happens to a deleted user?","It goes to **Deleted users** and can be **restored for 30 days** with its group memberships and licenses. After 30 days it is permanently deleted.")
Q(1,"You need users from the Marketing department to be added to a group automatically when their department attribute is set. What should you create?","A security group with dynamic user membership",["A security group with assigned membership","A Microsoft 365 group with assigned membership","An administrative unit"],"Dynamic user membership evaluates a rule on user attributes. It needs Microsoft Entra ID P1.")
Q(1,"You try to assign a Microsoft 365 license to a new user and the option is unavailable. What should you set first?","The user's usage location",["The user's job title","The user's manager","The user's department"],"Usage location is required for license assignment because not every service is offered in every country.")
Q(1,"A partner company's staff need access to one of your apps. They must use their own company credentials. What should you do?","Invite them as B2B guest users",["Create cloud-only member accounts for them","Sync their accounts with Microsoft Entra Connect","Create a Microsoft 365 group for them"],"B2B collaboration lets external users sign in with their own identity and appear as guests in your tenant.")
Q(1,"Which TWO can be members of a security group in Microsoft Entra ID?",["Devices","Other groups"],["Storage accounts","Subscriptions"],"Security groups can contain users, devices, service principals and other groups. Azure resources are not members.")
YN(1,["You can manually add a user to a group that has dynamic user membership.","Group-based licensing removes the license when a user leaves the group.","A deleted user can be restored within 30 days."],[0,1,1],"Dynamic groups are rule-only. Group licensing follows membership. Deleted users stay restorable for 30 days.")
Q(1,"You enable SSPR for a group named SSPR-Users. A Global Administrator who is not in the group forgets their password. What happens?","They can reset it with two methods, because admins are always enabled for SSPR",["They cannot use SSPR until added to SSPR-Users","They can reset it with one method","Only another Global Administrator can reset it, by design"],"Administrator roles always have SSPR on with a two-gate policy, whatever the SSPR scope.")
M(1,"Match each requirement to the group type or setting.",[("Shared mailbox and Teams for a project","Microsoft 365 group"),("Grant an Azure role to a set of users","Security group"),("Members added by department attribute","Dynamic user membership"),("All Windows devices added automatically","Dynamic device membership")],"Microsoft 365 groups are for collaboration. Security groups grant access. Dynamic rules can target users or devices, not both in one group.")
Q(1,"You need to create 500 user accounts from a spreadsheet with the least effort in the portal. What should you use?","Bulk create with the CSV template",["Invite users one by one","Microsoft Entra Connect Sync","An access review"],"Bulk create in the Entra admin center takes a CSV built from the template.")
Q(1,"Which license do you need to let cloud users reset forgotten passwords themselves?","Microsoft Entra ID P1",["Microsoft Entra ID Free","No license; it is included in every tenant","Microsoft Defender for Identity"],"SSPR reset needs P1 or higher. Changing a known password is free.")
D(1,"Security group","Microsoft 365 group","Gives a team a shared mailbox, calendar and SharePoint site.",1,"Microsoft 365 groups are for collaboration. Security groups grant access.")
D(1,"Assigned membership","Dynamic membership","Needs Microsoft Entra ID P1 and blocks manual adds.",1,"Dynamic groups are rule-based and premium.")
D(1,"Member user","Guest user","Signs in with their own organization's identity after an invitation.",1,"B2B guests keep their home identity.")
D(1,"Password change","Password reset","Needs Entra ID P1 for cloud users.",1,"Reset (forgotten password) is P1. Change (you know the old one) is free.")
# ---- 2 Access to Azure resources
C(2,"The four fundamental Azure built-in roles?","**Owner:** full access, including assigning roles. **Contributor:** full access to manage resources, **cannot assign roles**. **Reader:** view only. **User Access Administrator:** manage user access (role assignments) only.")
C(2,"Role Based Access Control Administrator?","Can **assign roles** (and can be limited with conditions to certain roles or principals), but cannot manage the resources themselves. A least-privilege alternative to Owner for delegating access.")
C(2,"The four Azure RBAC scopes, top to bottom?","**Management group → Subscription → Resource group → Resource.** A role assigned at a scope is **inherited** by everything below it.")
C(2,"What makes up a role assignment?","**Security principal** (user, group, service principal, managed identity) + **role definition** (what actions) + **scope** (where).")
C(2,"How do multiple role assignments combine?","**Additively.** Effective permissions are the union of all assignments. Reader at the subscription plus Contributor on one resource group = Contributor on that group, Reader everywhere else. **Deny assignments** win over allows.")
C(2,"Actions vs DataActions in a role definition?","**Actions** = management plane (create, delete, configure). **DataActions** = data plane (read blob contents, send queue messages). Owner does **not** automatically read blob data through Entra auth; you need roles such as **Storage Blob Data Reader**.")
C(2,"Azure roles vs Microsoft Entra roles?","**Azure roles** control Azure resources (VMs, storage, networks) at management group to resource scope. **Entra roles** control directory objects (users, groups, apps), for example Global Administrator or User Administrator. A Global Administrator can **elevate** to User Access Administrator at root scope.")
C(2,"Virtual Machine Contributor can do what?","Manage **virtual machines**, but **not** sign in to them and **not** manage the virtual network or storage account they connect to.")
C(2,"How do you check what someone can do?","Resource → **Access control (IAM)** → **Check access**, or the **Role assignments** tab. It shows direct and **inherited** assignments and the scope each came from.")
Q(2,"A user must create and manage all resources in a resource group but must not grant access to others. Which role should you assign at the resource group?","Contributor",["Owner","User Access Administrator","Reader"],"Contributor manages resources but cannot assign roles. Owner can assign roles.")
Q(2,"You assign Reader to User1 at the subscription and Contributor to User1 on RG1. What can User1 do on a VM in RG1?","Manage the VM",["Only view the VM","Nothing, because the assignments conflict","Assign roles on the VM"],"RBAC is additive. Contributor on RG1 is inherited by the VM.")
Q(2,"You must allow a help desk group to assign roles on RG1 without being able to change any resources. Which role is least privileged?","Role Based Access Control Administrator",["Owner","Contributor","Virtual Machine Contributor"],"RBAC Administrator can manage role assignments only. Owner can also change resources.")
Q(2,"Which TWO are valid scopes for an Azure role assignment?",["Management group","Resource group"],["Microsoft Entra administrative unit","Availability zone"],"Azure RBAC scopes are management group, subscription, resource group and resource.")
YN(2,["A role assigned at a subscription is inherited by every resource group in it.","Contributor can assign roles to other users.","The Owner role always lets a user read blob data when using Microsoft Entra authorization."],[1,0,0],"Inheritance flows down. Contributor cannot assign roles. Blob data access through Entra needs a data role such as Storage Blob Data Reader.")
M(2,"Match each need to the least-privileged built-in role.",[("View everything, change nothing","Reader"),("Manage resources, no role assignments","Contributor"),("Manage role assignments only","User Access Administrator"),("Read blobs with Entra ID","Storage Blob Data Reader")],"Pick the smallest role that does the job.")
Q(2,"An app running on a VM must read secrets from Azure Key Vault without storing credentials. Which security principal should receive the role?","The VM's managed identity",["The admin's user account","A Microsoft 365 group","The VM's network interface"],"A managed identity is a security principal Azure manages for the resource, so no secrets are stored.")
Q(2,"A user is Global Administrator in Microsoft Entra ID but cannot see any subscriptions. What can they do to manage access to all subscriptions?","Elevate access to become User Access Administrator at root scope",["Assign themselves the Reader role in Entra ID","Create a new tenant","Add themselves to a Microsoft 365 group"],"Entra roles do not grant Azure resource access. Global Administrators can elevate access to the root scope.")
D(2,"Owner","Contributor","Can manage resources AND assign roles.",0,"Owner = Contributor plus role assignment.")
D(2,"Azure role","Microsoft Entra role","User Administrator, which resets passwords for directory users.",1,"Entra roles manage directory objects.")
D(2,"Actions","DataActions","Reading the contents of a blob.",1,"Data-plane operations are DataActions.")
D(2,"Reader at subscription","Contributor at resource group","Effective permission on a VM inside that resource group.",1,"Assignments add up: Contributor wins in that group.")
# ---- 3 Subscriptions and governance
C(3,"Azure Policy vs RBAC?","**RBAC:** *who* can do *what* actions. **Policy:** *what* resources may look like, whoever creates them (allowed regions, required tags, allowed SKUs). Policy can deny even an Owner.")
C(3,"Common Azure Policy effects?","**Deny** (block the request), **Audit** (log non-compliance), **Append** / **Modify** (add or change properties such as tags), **AuditIfNotExists** / **DeployIfNotExists** (check or deploy a related resource), **Disabled**.")
C(3,"Policy definition vs initiative vs assignment?","**Definition:** one rule. **Initiative:** a group of definitions managed together. **Assignment:** applies a definition or initiative to a scope, with optional **exclusions** and parameters.")
C(3,"What happens to existing resources when you assign a Deny policy?","They are **not deleted or changed**. They show as **non-compliant**. Fix them with a **remediation task** (for Modify and DeployIfNotExists, which use a **managed identity**) or by hand.")
C(3,"The two resource lock types?","**CanNotDelete (Delete):** can read and modify, cannot delete. **ReadOnly:** can read, cannot modify or delete. Locks are **inherited** by child resources and apply to **everyone, including Owners**.")
C(3,"Who can create or remove locks?","Anyone with `Microsoft.Authorization/locks/*`: **Owner** and **User Access Administrator** among built-in roles. Contributor cannot.")
C(3,"Are tags inherited?","**No.** A tag on a resource group or subscription is **not** applied to the resources in it. Use Azure Policy (for example *Inherit a tag from the resource group*, a **Modify** policy) to copy tags. Up to **50 tags** per resource.")
C(3,"Key resource group rules?","A resource is in **exactly one** resource group. The group has a location for its **metadata**, but its resources can be in **any region**. Deleting a group **deletes everything in it**. Resource groups cannot be nested.")
C(3,"Management groups: limits?","Organize subscriptions for policy and RBAC. A **root management group** per tenant. Up to **six levels** of depth below root (not counting the subscription level). Each subscription and management group has **one parent**.")
C(3,"Budgets vs cost alerts vs Advisor?","**Budget:** a spending limit with alert thresholds (actual or forecasted). It **does not stop resources** by itself; it can trigger an **action group**. **Cost alerts:** budget, credit and quota alerts, plus anomaly alerts. **Azure Advisor:** recommendations such as resizing or shutting down underused VMs and buying reservations.")
Q(3,"You must prevent anyone, including subscription Owners, from deleting a production resource group, while still allowing changes to its resources. What should you apply?","A CanNotDelete lock on the resource group",["A ReadOnly lock on the resource group","Remove the Owner role from all users","An Azure Policy with the Audit effect"],"CanNotDelete blocks deletion but allows modification, and it applies to Owners too.")
Q(3,"You need to make sure resources can only be created in East US and West US. What should you use?","Azure Policy with the Allowed locations definition",["A resource lock","An RBAC custom role","A management group tag"],"Policy controls resource properties such as location, whatever role the creator has.")
Q(3,"A Department tag is set on RG1. A new storage account is created in RG1. What tags does the storage account have?","None, unless a policy or the creator adds them",["Department, inherited from RG1","All tags of the subscription","Department, but only after 24 hours"],"Tags are not inherited. Use a Modify policy to inherit them.")
Q(3,"Which TWO policy effects can change or create resources through a remediation task?",["Modify","DeployIfNotExists"],["Audit","Deny"],"Modify and DeployIfNotExists use a managed identity and remediation tasks. Audit only reports, Deny only blocks.")
YN(3,["A ReadOnly lock on a resource group stops you from creating a new VM in it.","A budget automatically shuts down resources when the limit is reached.","Resources in a resource group can be in different regions from the group."],[1,0,1],"ReadOnly blocks writes. Budgets alert and can trigger actions but do not stop resources by themselves. Resource group location only holds metadata.")
M(3,"Match each requirement to the governance tool.",[("Block VMs larger than a set size","Azure Policy"),("Stop accidental deletion of a database","Resource lock"),("Alert when forecasted spend passes 80%","Budget"),("Recommend resizing underused VMs","Azure Advisor")],"Policy shapes resources. Locks protect them. Budgets watch spend. Advisor recommends.")
Q(3,"You need to apply the same policies and role assignments to 30 subscriptions. What should you configure?","A management group that contains the subscriptions",["A resource group in each subscription","A tag on each subscription","A single resource lock"],"Assignments at a management group are inherited by all subscriptions under it.")
Q(3,"A storage account has a ReadOnly lock. An admin with Owner tries to list the access keys in the portal and fails. Why?","Listing keys is a POST (write) operation that ReadOnly blocks",["Owners cannot read storage keys","The keys were rotated","The lock is only on the resource group"],"List Keys is a POST action, so ReadOnly blocks it even for Owners.")
D(3,"Azure Policy","Azure RBAC","Controls which SKUs may be deployed, whoever deploys them.",0,"Policy governs resource properties. RBAC governs who can act.")
D(3,"CanNotDelete lock","ReadOnly lock","Allows changes but blocks deletion.",0,"ReadOnly blocks changes too.")
D(3,"Budget","Azure Advisor","Recommends buying reserved instances to save money.",1,"Advisor recommends. Budgets alert on spend.")
D(3,"Policy initiative","Management group","A container that groups subscriptions.",1,"An initiative groups policy definitions. A management group groups subscriptions.")
# ---- 4 Access to storage
C(4,"Storage firewall: default action and options?","Set public network access to **Enabled from selected virtual networks and IP addresses**. Allow **VNet subnets** (needs a **Microsoft.Storage service endpoint**), **public IP ranges** (not private RFC 1918 addresses), **resource instances**, and **trusted Microsoft services** as an exception.")
C(4,"Storage account access keys?","Two keys, **key1 and key2**, each gives **full access** to the account. Rotate one while apps use the other. Store them in **Key Vault**. You can **disallow Shared Key** authorization to force Entra ID.")
C(4,"The three SAS types?","**User delegation SAS:** signed with **Microsoft Entra** credentials; Blob and Data Lake only; **recommended**. **Service SAS:** signed with the **account key**, one service. **Account SAS:** signed with the account key, **one or more services**, plus service-level operations.")
C(4,"What is in a SAS token?","Signed fields such as **sp** (permissions), **st/se** (start and expiry), **sip** (allowed IPs), **spr** (HTTPS only), **sr** (resource) and the **sig** signature. Anyone holding the URL has that access until it expires.")
C(4,"Stored access policy?","Defined on a **container, file share, queue or table**. A **service SAS** can reference it for start, expiry and permissions. **Max five per container.** Revoke every SAS that uses it by **deleting or changing the policy**, without rotating keys.")
C(4,"How do you revoke an ad hoc service SAS with no stored access policy?","**Regenerate the account key** that signed it (or wait for expiry). That breaks every SAS and app using that key.")
C(4,"Azure Files identity-based access: the three identity sources?","**On-premises AD DS** (hybrid users synced to Entra), **Microsoft Entra Domain Services**, **Microsoft Entra Kerberos** (no line of sight to a domain controller needed). **One source per storage account.** Kerberos must be enabled in SMB security settings.")
C(4,"Share-level vs file-level permissions in Azure Files?","**Share level:** Azure RBAC roles such as **Storage File Data SMB Share Reader / Contributor / Elevated Contributor**, or a **default share-level permission** for all authenticated users. **Directory and file level:** Windows **NTFS ACLs**. Both must allow access.")
C(4,"Azure Files over SMB: which port must be open?","**TCP 445** outbound. Many ISPs block it; use VPN, ExpressRoute or Azure File Sync if so.")
Q(4,"A contractor needs read access to one container for 48 hours. You must be able to revoke the access early without affecting other apps that use the account keys. What should you use?","A service SAS that references a stored access policy",["An account SAS","Share the storage account key","Regenerate key1 after 48 hours"],"Deleting or changing the stored access policy revokes the SAS without rotating keys.")
Q(4,"Which SAS type is signed with Microsoft Entra credentials and recommended by Microsoft?","User delegation SAS",["Account SAS","Service SAS","Ad hoc SAS"],"A user delegation SAS uses a key obtained with Entra credentials instead of the account key.")
Q(4,"VMs in Subnet1 must reach a storage account while all other networks are blocked. What should you configure on Subnet1 and the storage account?","A Microsoft.Storage service endpoint and a virtual network rule",["A NAT gateway and an IP rule for 10.0.1.0/24","An NSG rule allowing port 443","A user-defined route to the internet"],"Storage virtual network rules need the subnet's service endpoint. Private IP ranges cannot be used in IP rules.")
Q(4,"Which TWO identity sources can provide identity-based SMB access to Azure Files?",["On-premises Active Directory Domain Services","Microsoft Entra Kerberos"],["Azure Key Vault","Microsoft Entra B2C local accounts"],"Azure Files supports AD DS, Entra Domain Services and Entra Kerberos.")
YN(4,["A stored access policy can be used with a user delegation SAS.","A container can have up to five stored access policies.","Each storage account access key grants full access to the account."],[0,1,1],"Stored access policies work with service SAS only. Five per container. Account keys are all-powerful.")
M(4,"Match each requirement to the access method.",[("Revoke many SAS tokens without changing keys","Stored access policy"),("SAS signed with Entra credentials","User delegation SAS"),("One SAS for blobs and queues together","Account SAS"),("Grant an SMB share to an AD group","Storage File Data SMB Share Contributor")],"Pick by what signs the token and what it covers.")
Q(4,"Users mount an Azure file share with AD credentials. They can connect but get Access denied on one folder. Share-level roles are correct. What should you check?","The NTFS permissions on the folder",["The storage account firewall","The SAS expiry time","The blob container access level"],"After the share-level check, Windows ACLs decide directory and file access.")
Q(4,"An ad hoc service SAS signed with key1 has leaked. There is no stored access policy. What revokes it immediately?","Regenerate key1",["Regenerate key2","Delete the container's lifecycle rule","Disable soft delete"],"Without a policy, the only way to invalidate the signature is to rotate the key that signed it.")
D(4,"Service SAS","Account SAS","Covers blobs and queues in one token.",1,"Account SAS can span services.")
D(4,"Stored access policy","Regenerate key","Revokes SAS tokens without breaking apps that use the keys.",0,"Changing the policy only affects SAS tokens tied to it.")
D(4,"Share-level permission","NTFS ACL","Uses Azure RBAC roles such as Storage File Data SMB Share Reader.",0,"Share level is RBAC. File level is NTFS.")
D(4,"Service endpoint","IP network rule","Lets a VNet subnet reach the storage account over its private address.",0,"Private RFC 1918 addresses cannot be used in IP rules.")
# ---- 5 Storage accounts
C(5,"Storage account types?","**Standard general-purpose v2** (blobs, files, queues, tables; most uses). **Premium block blobs**, **Premium file shares**, **Premium page blobs** (SSD, low latency, one service each).")
C(5,"LRS, ZRS, GRS, GZRS?","**LRS:** 3 copies in one datacenter. **ZRS:** 3 copies across **availability zones**. **GRS:** LRS plus an async copy (LRS) in the **paired region**. **GZRS:** ZRS plus a copy in the paired region. Add **RA-** for **read access** to the secondary.")
C(5,"Which redundancy survives what?","LRS: a rack or drive. **ZRS:** a whole **zone** (datacenter). **GRS/GZRS:** a whole **region**. **RA-GRS/RA-GZRS:** read from the secondary **without** waiting for failover.")
C(5,"Premium storage redundancy options?","Premium accounts support **LRS and ZRS** only. No geo-redundancy.")
C(5,"What can't you change after creating a storage account?","The **name** (globally unique, 3-24 lowercase letters and numbers) and the **region**. The **performance tier** (Standard vs Premium) also cannot be changed. Redundancy can be changed, sometimes needing a conversion.")
C(5,"Object replication requirements?","Copies **block blobs** asynchronously between accounts. Needs **versioning on both** accounts and **change feed on the source**. GPv2 or premium block blob. Not with **hierarchical namespace**. **Snapshots are not replicated.** Archive tier blobs break replication.")
C(5,"Storage encryption basics?","**Always on**, AES-256, cannot be disabled. Keys: **Microsoft-managed** (default) or **customer-managed** in **Key Vault** or Managed HSM (the vault needs **soft delete and purge protection**). **Infrastructure encryption** (double) must be chosen **at creation**. **Encryption scopes** use different keys per container or blob.")
C(5,"AzCopy vs Storage Explorer?","**AzCopy:** command line for fast copy and **sync** to and from blobs and files (`azcopy copy`, `azcopy sync`), auth with Entra or SAS. **Storage Explorer:** desktop GUI to browse and manage blobs, files, queues and tables.")
C(5,"Hierarchical namespace?","Turns blob storage into **Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2**: real directories and POSIX ACLs for analytics. Some blob features (for example object replication) are not supported with it.")
Q(5,"Data must survive the loss of an entire Azure region and be readable from the secondary region at any time. Which redundancy should you choose?","RA-GRS",["ZRS","LRS","GRS"],"RA-GRS replicates to the paired region and allows reads from the secondary without failover. GRS needs failover first.")
Q(5,"You need the lowest-cost redundancy that survives the failure of one datacenter (zone) in the region. What should you choose?","ZRS",["LRS","GRS","RA-GZRS"],"ZRS copies across zones. LRS stays in one datacenter. Geo options cost more.")
Q(5,"You plan object replication from storage1 to storage2. Which TWO settings are required on storage1?",["Blob versioning","Change feed"],["Hierarchical namespace","Infrastructure encryption"],"The source needs versioning and change feed. The destination needs versioning.")
Q(5,"You must use your own keys to encrypt a storage account. Where must the key be stored?","Azure Key Vault or Managed HSM",["In the storage account's access keys","In a blob container","In an app setting"],"Customer-managed keys live in Key Vault or Managed HSM, with soft delete and purge protection on.")
YN(5,["You can turn off encryption at rest for a standard storage account.","Infrastructure (double) encryption can be enabled after the account is created.","Premium file shares support zone-redundant storage."],[0,0,1],"Encryption is always on. Infrastructure encryption is set at creation. Premium supports LRS and ZRS.")
M(5,"Match each copy of data to the redundancy option.",[("3 copies in one datacenter","LRS"),("3 copies across availability zones","ZRS"),("Copies in the paired region, readable any time","RA-GRS"),("Zone copies plus a paired region copy","GZRS")],"Count where the copies live.")
Q(5,"You need to copy 2 TB from an on-premises file server to a blob container from a script, and re-run it later copying only changes. What should you use?","AzCopy with the sync command",["Azure Storage Explorer","The Azure portal upload button","Object replication"],"AzCopy is scriptable and azcopy sync copies only differences.")
Q(5,"Which storage account type should you choose for Azure file shares that need consistent low latency on SSDs?","Premium file shares (FileStorage)",["Standard general-purpose v2","Premium page blobs","Premium block blobs"],"Premium file shares are the SSD account kind for Azure Files.")
D(5,"GRS","RA-GRS","Lets apps read from the secondary region without a failover.",1,"RA = read access.")
D(5,"LRS","ZRS","Survives the loss of one availability zone.",1,"ZRS spreads copies across zones.")
D(5,"AzCopy","Storage Explorer","A desktop GUI to browse containers and shares.",1,"AzCopy is the command line tool.")
D(5,"Microsoft-managed keys","Customer-managed keys","Needs Key Vault with purge protection.",1,"CMK keys live in your vault.")
